      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q110",
      "answer": "It may use the eligible Innate at its proper speed: unless explicitly specified otherwise it costs no Energy and no Card Play and is not a card played from hand. Innates are automatically available every turn when their requirements are met. Ordinary once-per-turn and targeting rules still apply.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.14 Spirit panel item 9; p.16 Powers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q111",
      "answer": "No to both. Ordinary Powers have one use per turn; paying again grants no second use. Making Slow Fast changes that use's timing, not its number: use it in Fast only, with no separate Slow-phase use. Additional uses require an explicit effect such as Repeat.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.17 One Land! One Turn! One Use! bullet 3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q112",
      "answer": "Randomly choose one balanced Island Board per Spirit and join them into the island. Populate every land according to its printed Invader, Dahan and Blight icons, taking setup Blight from the box rather than depleting the pool; setup Blight does not cascade or destroy Presence. Shuffle Minor and Major decks separately, each with its own shared discard space, and put Energy, Invaders and Dahan in shared supplies accessible to players.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.6 Island and Supply; pp.13,15",
        "FAQ Setup: .9v5ka5b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q113",
      "answer": "Ocean In Play Pushes the surviving Dahan to a non-Ocean land as part of its own triggered action. This is an actual Push, capable of triggering applicable movement effects; it is not the later non-action cleanup operation. Cleanup only handles a piece still illegally placed after the action tree. No expansion effect or piece is needed for this branch: the FAQ expressly supplies Infinite Vitality threshold on the Ocean as a core-game case.",
      "source_refs": [
        "FAQ Core: .9v5kfqs; .7w4gdtk; .bu6ocxx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q114",
      "answer": "It need not keep its original target. The Spirit may choose any valid target by the ordinary Range and Target rules, either the original land or a different legal land. Only a Repeat that specifies its destination replaces those normal restrictions with the specified-location instruction.",
      "source_refs": [
        "CORE p.19 Repeat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q115",
      "answer": "The Invaders deal 3 Damage to land, adding one Blight; Concealing Shadows protects only Dahan and does not reduce land Damage. The Dahan take zero Damage and both survive healthy, then counterattack for 4 total Damage. They may destroy the Town (2 Health) and Explorer (1), with excess Damage unused, generating 1 Fear from the Town during this Ravage. The Power’s earlier printed Fear is separate from the requested Ravage-generated Fear.",
